      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">DESTINATION PROTOCOL</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Doorstep Delivery Handover, Inventory Verification &amp; Placement at Kakinada</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>The final delivery and uncrating protocol at Kakinada is executed with precision to ensure asset integrity and immediate operational readiness. The process begins strictly during daylight hours, allowing for clear visual inspection and accurate verification. Upon arrival, the receiving team conducts a comprehensive cross-check of the physical inventory against the original bilty documents.</p>
<p>This step is critical to confirm that all listed items are present and undamaged during transit. Any discrepancies in quantity or visible external damage must be documented immediately on the delivery challan before the driver departs, ensuring clear liability and facilitating swift reconciliation.</p>

<p>Once the inventory is verified, the uncrating process commences, focusing on the careful extraction of goods. Special attention is given to electrical and mechanical items. Before any equipment is installed or plugged in, a preliminary functional test is performed.</p>
<p>Technicians verify that all components are intact, free from moisture ingress, and that basic mechanical movements are smooth. For electrical units, a safe, low-power check is conducted to ensure no short circuits exist before full commissioning. This proactive testing prevents costly post-installation failures and ensures that only fully operational assets enter the active workflow.</p>

<p>Simultaneously, the placement of clean furniture is handled with meticulous care. Items are positioned exactly according to the pre-approved layout plan, ensuring optimal workflow and aesthetic consistency.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Furniture is inspected for scratches or dents that may have occurred during unpacking, and any necessary protective coverings are removed only after final positioning is confirmed.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This stage emphasizes a pristine environment, reflecting the high standards of the Kakinada facility and ensuring that the workspace is ready for immediate use without the need for additional cleaning or adjustments.</span></li></ul>

<p>Finally, the swift and systematic removal of packing debris is a non-negotiable step in the protocol. All cartons, foam, bubble wrap, and wooden crates are consolidated and removed from the premises within two hours of uncrating completion. This rapid cleanup prevents clutter, reduces trip hazards, and maintains a professional appearance.</p>
<p>The discarded materials are segregated for recycling or disposal according to local environmental regulations. By adhering to this rigorous protocol, the Kakinada team ensures a seamless transition from delivery to operational status, minimizing downtime and upholding the highest standards of logistical efficiency and site hygiene.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



